== THE EDGES THAT DECIDE ORDERING ==

  CM6 before editor multi-buffer, or multi-buffer gets built twice.
  OPFS store before the includes resolver, or SourceLoader gets written twice.

  D -> E -> OPFS store -> library UI + zip export is what turns this into a tool
  someone other than its author can use. Everything in the editor chain is
  quality of life on top of an authoring loop that does not exist yet.

  F is pure measurement - it retires an open question rather than building
  anything. H was the other one, and it is settled: see the note at the top.


== UNSEQUENCED ==

  Nothing below came out of the design docs; no dependencies claimed.

  NVL mode

  Note (text message) system
    TextBoxType has only ADV, with a "todo maybe note at some point" comment.

  Text node parsing (colors, text speed)
    TextNode already carries color and characterDelay, but Say hardcodes
    characterDelay: 20 and takes the colour from the actor. Nothing parses
    per-node markup.

  Sprites
    Sprite flipping
    Position presets   - ShowCommandSchema accepts `position` and apply()
                         ignores it entirely

  Decision showIf
    Show/hide individual decision options based on variables.

  Arbitrary transformation matrix for backgrounds
    Currently pan and scale via four-number viewboxes.

  Rewrite the audio renderer against WebAudioContext
    To close the Chrome gapless-looping problem.
